[TGW construction]
Let $n\in\Z_{>0}$, $(R,\si,t)$ be an object in $\TGW{n}{\K}$, and $\mu\in\PM{n}{\K}$.
The twisted generalized Weyl construction with parameter matrix $\mu$
associated to the TGW datum $(R,\si,t)$ is denoted by $\TGWC{R}{\si}{t}{\mu}$
and is defined as the free $R$-ring on the set $\{x_i,y_i\mid i=1,\ldots,n\}$
modulo the two-sided ideal generated by the following set of elements:

\begin{subequations}
\begin{alignat}{3}
x_ir  &-\si_i(r)x_i,  &\quad y_ir&-\si_i^{-1}(r)y_i,
&\quad \text{$\forall r\in R,\, i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}$,} \\
y_ix_i&-t_i, &\quad x_iy_i&-\si_i(t_i),
&\quad \text{$\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}$,} \\
&&\quad x_iy_j&-\mu_{ij}y_jx_i,
&\quad \text{$\forall i,j\in\{1,\ldots,n\},\, i\neq j$.}
\end{alignat}
\end{subequations}
